ic tip but  something very important as well to keep  in mind there are too many people who  have seen placing bushes on the other  side of the map then where you actually  see anything which is a waste of Polly's  and a waste of your time so it's  definitely something that I would avoid  and I generally go less detailed as you  go further away from the point where you  actually see everything also to save a  bit of time I saved a blueprint over  here which is something that I  definitely recommend anyone doing if you  have a large space to fill with trees  just place a cup of them make a  blueprint out of it and you can save  yourself a lot of time in the long run  there are so many things which blue  prints are amazing for and at this point  I feel like the ride is really coming  together especially from the lake it has  an almost finished look to it I just had  this unfinished corner which still don't  have any rocks and foliage and then  there's the area with the station but it  doesn't really impact the look at the  right that much this was the first thing  that I wanted to tackle and actually  finish this area over here where again I  wanted to leave some open spaces but not  necessarily because I didn't want to  fill everything with forests but also  because there are some sight lines that  I feel are very important over here that  I wanted to preserve at all costs so the  first one is from the queue just before  you enter the little roof building on  the queue if you look over the lake  there's gonna be this open place where  there aren't any trees blocking the view  and then in the distance you can see  this rock looming up basically the same  kind of goes from the main path as you  approach the station from the park  entrance you'll actually be able to see  this rock kind of loom up in the  distance between the station and the  loop of the coaster so I wanted to keep  that sight line open as well so there  aren't too many trees around there but  it's definitely in a very important  place and it's gonna be much more  important once I add the wingy on top of  it but before that there's still no of  the attending to do so the first thing  that I wanted to do here is work a bit  on the general area for the  which is not too interesting just you  know it's an unfinished area there  aren't any trees or any scenery so I  wanted to fix that but what is  interesting is that this is also where I  built my quick Christmas tree I didn't  want to go over the top  the guests are absolutely going bonkers  for that little part of there but I  didn't want to go over the top for the  Christmas tree I just wanted to have a  few decorations in there but not just  you know populate it too much with all  of these Christmas bells and stuff so  it's quite simple but I didn't want to  use an in-game regular tree and then  that created myself so that there's  still a few of those snow coverings and  at least to give it a bit of a personal  touch I personally do like red  decorations and I don't know why people  even have silver decorations in  Christmas trees it's just too colourless  like what are you even doing so I wanted  to have some colorful decorations in  here generally I'm just switching it up  between two types of the Christmas balls  I don't know what you actually call them  in English and then there's the  Christmas bells and of course the stone  on top and of course some big presence  at the bottom like really huge presents  so that should give any pretty cool  festive kind of atmosphere to this  entire area I suppose there are of  course be other other kind of  decorations you know like these rocks in  the foliage but also barrels any kind of  any kind of thing that you might see  stored around areas like this but it's  the Christmas thing and the Christmas  tree and the Christmas decorations and  of course presents that I feel make it  the most Christmas kind of atmosphere so  that's the most important part I would  say of the detailing here now with that  out of the way all that was still left  to do is foliage but that's boring so  let's skip ahead and go into the very  final thing of this video which is the  hut on top of the hill now I want to say  I wanted to keep this as simple as I  could because I didn't have that much  time left at this point and well I also  just recycled the parts that I made  earlier on and at this point I basically  saved every custom-made modular piece  time  made so I have a pretty solid collection  of different custom Russian pieces at  this point and all I still have to do is  just put these things together in a most  of the kind of sense that actually  wasn't that much work because most of  the work for this building has already  been done upfront in making these custom  pieces so it's very simple Hut's I just  put the roof pieces together that I  already had the only thing that I wanted  to do with this thing that was slightly  more complicated is the onion Tower and  I got so many requests to do this kind  of thing actually considered it right  from the start from episode 1 you've got  like these famous Russian onion and bell  towers with the spiraling collars you  know like you see on many Russian  landmarks and it's something that you  definitely see in some of these more  traditional smaller wooden huts as well  especially in theme parks it's a very  fancy addition I was just very afraid of  making these things since you know  they're onion towers and one of the  hardest things to make if not the  hardest things to make custom when it  comes to spires so in the end I just  decided to go for a very small one that  fits the simple wooden Outback kind of  atmosphere of the build and make it in a  simple way as well just make one outline  and copy that into the shape that I need  and that is basically it and that is  also more or less its for this episode  so I really want to thank you guys for  watching this and I want to thank you  guys for watching this entire series  it's been awesome have a Merry Christmas  and if I don't see you any more  a happy 2017 as well and stay tuned for  the POV video see you later guys  [Music]
 

